description: Never use hyphenated compound words in Spires pages or UI copy
alwaysApply: true
---

# No hyphenated compounds in pages and UI

Never join words with a hyphen in customer or admin facing copy, labels, buttons, emails, or website pages.

Do not write forms such as `8-seater`, `customer-facing`, `four-passenger`, `pre-booked`, `payment-method`, or `no-show` in UI text.

Write them as separate words: `8 seater`, `customer facing`, `four passenger`, `pre booked`, `payment method`, `no show`.

Code identifiers, URLs, CSS classes, and Firestore field names may keep hyphens or underscores. Visible language must not.

```html
<!-- BAD -->
<p>Shared 8-seater transfer. Customer-facing status.</p>

<!-- GOOD -->
<p>Shared 8 seater transfer. Customer facing status.</p>
```
